# Task: Power/signal strap stack — spec and height/width calculation

## Context
I am planning a horizontal routing stack of power and signal straps. All dimensions are in microns (µm).
Do not assume any value not given here. If something needed is marked <TBD>, ask me before proceeding.

## Track rules
- Wire width: 0.72 µm (every net, power and signal)
- Spacing between adjacent wires: 0.72 µm (edge to edge)
- Track pitch: 1.44 µm (width + spacing)
- Same width/spacing applies in X and Y
- Metal layer: <TBD, e.g. M7 horizontal>
- Tool / PDK: <TBD, e.g. Innovus / ICC2, node>

## Stack order (top to bottom), 7 tracks
1. VSS        (added extra)
2. VDD_SOC
3. SIGNAL
4. VSS
5. SIGNAL
6. VDD_SOC
7. VDD_SOC    (added extra)

## Height requirement
- Edge-to-edge height = 7 × 0.72 + 6 × 0.72 = 9.36 µm
- Tileable height (half spacing, 0.36 µm, above and below) = 7 × 1.44 = 10.08 µm
- Use 10.08 µm if the stack repeats or abuts other routing; 9.36 µm if it is isolated.

## Width requirement
- Straps run horizontally, so width = strap length.
- Strap length / span: <TBD, e.g. full macro width, X µm, or N repetitions>
- If the same 7-track pattern is also used vertically on the orthogonal layer,
  width = 9.36 µm edge to edge / 10.08 µm tileable.

## Open items to flag (do not silently resolve)
1. Tracks 6 and 7 are both VDD_SOC and adjacent. Either keep as two straps
   or merge into one 2.16 µm strap (0.72 + 0.72 + 0.72). Ask me which.
   If merged, check the PDK wide-metal spacing rule, which may exceed 0.72 µm.
2. Confirm 0.72 µm spacing is legal for 0.72 µm wide power straps on this layer
   (wide-metal / PRL spacing rules).
3. Confirm the stack aligns to the routing track grid / manufacturing grid.

## What I want from you
1. Restate the spec back to me and list any assumptions.
2. Compute the height (both edge-to-edge and tileable) and the width once the span is known,
   showing the arithmetic.
3. Produce: <TBD — e.g. a table of each net's y-offset (bottom and top edge),
   and/or tool commands (addStripe / create_pg_strap) to create the straps>.
4. List any rule checks I should run afterward (DRC spacing, grid alignment).
